AbandonResponse.description:
The abandon brief (D8): what was torn down + the children triage list. Blocking children
existed only for this parent — the owner disposes each (abandon / promote to independent);
parallel children continue untouched.

RunEventRow.description:
One entry of a run's event trail: a prompt, an assistant reply block, a tool/skill/agent call,
or that call's `result`. `kind` ∈ prompt | reply | tool | mcp | skill | agent | subagent | result;
`name` is the label, `description` the body; `tool_id` pairs a result back to its call.

SpawnedFrom.description:
The D3 provenance edge, child-side: which item this one branched off and how. `blocking`/
`parallel` = real children (gate the parent's completion; blocking also pauses it);
`spawn` = provenance-only follow-up. Exactly one origin edge per item; parent views derived.
